WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:05.690
School Festival in 7 Days

00:15.910 --> 00:17.040
Are you performing live?

00:17.040 --> 00:18.280
I'll be there!

00:18.280 --> 00:19.120
So awesome.

00:19.120 --> 00:20.700
Can I get a photo with you?

00:28.660 --> 00:29.920
I'll be there, too.

00:30.640 --> 00:34.240
I'm actually working on
an original song, too.

00:34.240 --> 00:36.840
I finally get a chance to show it off.

00:36.840 --> 00:39.900
Kagura Sousuke here's
going to raise the roof.

00:39.900 --> 00:41.310
See you there!

00:42.810 --> 00:44.890
Hey! I'm serious!

00:44.890 --> 00:46.430
I'm actually going to be there!

00:46.430 --> 00:47.730
You're all talk again.

00:48.110 --> 00:49.420
Kagura? A band?

00:49.420 --> 00:50.260
Is that a joke?

00:50.260 --> 00:51.580
Hilarious.

00:51.940 --> 00:53.580
No, I'm serious.

00:53.580 --> 00:54.680
I'll be performing.

00:54.680 --> 00:56.600
I have an awesome song ready.

00:56.600 --> 00:58.940
Sure, sure, I can't wait.

00:59.770 --> 01:01.630
Just watch me.

02:34.600 --> 02:35.670
Please!

02:35.980 --> 02:37.670
Start a band with me!

02:38.050 --> 02:39.060
I'm begging you.

02:38.550 --> 02:43.550
15: "School Festival from Hell"

02:39.060 --> 02:40.230
Biggest favor ever!

02:40.230 --> 02:44.230
I already declared it, so I have
to start a band with you guys now.

02:44.230 --> 02:47.630
I, Kagura Sousuke, have no other options!

02:44.790 --> 02:45.530
Five.

02:45.530 --> 02:48.270
One, two, three, four...

02:47.020 --> 02:48.270
Dumped by your girlfriend
Lose one turn

02:49.400 --> 02:51.690
I lose a turn?! Why?!

02:52.710 --> 02:54.280
That's a sad sight, Wolf.

02:54.280 --> 02:56.210
You'll have to wait patiently.

02:56.210 --> 02:59.660
It looks like you're having a hard
time getting married, though, Senpai.

03:00.250 --> 03:02.070
That's uncalled for!

03:02.070 --> 03:03.630
You haven't gotten married, either.

03:04.870 --> 03:06.490
Where'd you end up, Cho-chan?

03:06.490 --> 03:09.120
Massive Heartbreak
Return to the beginning

03:07.490 --> 03:10.060
Oh, dear, Cho-chan.

03:13.350 --> 03:14.340
Hey, stop that!

03:14.340 --> 03:16.750
Move your feet!

03:17.310 --> 03:19.890
Please, Beethes-sensei.

03:19.890 --> 03:21.670
Let's start a band together.

03:21.670 --> 03:24.020
Wolf! You don't get to go for a turn.

03:24.020 --> 03:25.050
Boo.

03:25.050 --> 03:27.050
Please, Master Motes, let's start a band.

03:27.050 --> 03:27.660
Please.

03:27.660 --> 03:30.180
Hurry up already. I'm bored.

03:30.530 --> 03:32.560
Liszt-sama, a band.

03:32.560 --> 03:35.050
Oh, my, I've had another child.

03:35.050 --> 03:36.400
Celebration!

03:36.950 --> 03:38.690
Prince Chopin!

03:37.150 --> 03:38.690
Massive heartbreak... Beginning...

03:39.010 --> 03:40.790
Professor Schu!

03:40.790 --> 03:44.280
Say, guys, you're living
it up here, aren't you?

03:44.280 --> 03:47.740
Would you mind taking a break from playing
and helping with the chores a little?

03:47.740 --> 03:49.700
I got married!

03:49.700 --> 03:50.930
What?!

03:50.930 --> 03:52.580
Are you listening?

03:52.580 --> 03:54.790
Come on, Kanae, tell them.

03:54.790 --> 03:57.440
I need to start a band with them.

04:01.060 --> 04:03.500
I won 100 million in the lottery!

04:03.500 --> 04:05.280
Damn it, you're so noisy.

04:05.280 --> 04:06.430
We're in the middle of dinner.

04:06.980 --> 04:09.500
Guys, would you please listen to me?

04:09.500 --> 04:11.250
Play with us, Kanae.

04:11.250 --> 04:12.980
Why would I?

04:12.980 --> 04:14.840
I'm not a kid.

04:16.020 --> 04:18.290
Don't say that.

04:17.720 --> 04:18.590
Please.

04:19.110 --> 04:20.440
Your pet chicken lays a golden
egg worth 1 billion!

04:20.440 --> 04:21.950
Yay!

04:21.950 --> 04:24.660
My pet chicken lays a golden
egg worth 1 billion!

04:25.030 --> 04:26.690
Say what?

04:27.660 --> 04:29.200
Guys!

04:30.130 --> 04:31.320
Listen to me!

04:31.320 --> 04:33.300
I've been talking this whole time!

04:33.300 --> 04:36.470
Shut up. We heard you, tool.

04:36.470 --> 04:40.000
Are you that desperate to play
this game with us, Kagura-kun?

04:40.000 --> 04:41.000
What?

04:41.000 --> 04:42.690
You weren't listening!

04:42.690 --> 04:44.170
I want you to start a band with me.

04:44.170 --> 04:45.650
No, Sousuke.

04:46.250 --> 04:48.460
You want to be part of
the school festival with them?

04:48.460 --> 04:50.100
I won't allow it.

04:50.100 --> 04:52.180
Who knows what kind of
incident it could cause.

04:53.530 --> 04:55.480
Would you perform with me, then?

04:55.700 --> 04:56.940
Me?

04:59.860 --> 05:01.940
No way. That's crazy.

05:02.740 --> 05:04.010
That sounds good.

05:04.010 --> 05:05.520
You should join him, Kanae.

05:05.520 --> 05:06.820
Snapadoll! Snapadoll!

05:12.920 --> 05:14.730
What was that for?!

05:14.730 --> 05:17.310
My car!

05:17.310 --> 05:21.300
I could totally kill it, if I started
a band with these geniuses.

05:21.880 --> 05:25.060
And you could all use your Musik.

05:25.060 --> 05:28.560
I'd be so popular.

05:29.610 --> 05:30.670
Sousuke...

05:31.020 --> 05:32.310
What did you just say?

05:34.550 --> 05:37.190
That you could be popular?

05:38.190 --> 05:39.540
No, Motes.

05:39.540 --> 05:40.440
No, no.

05:40.440 --> 05:41.620
Never.

05:41.620 --> 05:43.220
No grinning.

05:43.220 --> 05:44.440
Motes!

05:44.440 --> 05:46.700
School Festival in 6 Days

05:46.700 --> 05:48.610
Cosplay Café

05:47.100 --> 05:48.610
Hey, hey, what do you think?

05:51.390 --> 05:53.120
You're so cute, Motes!

05:54.190 --> 05:55.230
Well?

05:55.230 --> 05:56.370
Oh, my God!

05:57.640 --> 05:58.790
Does this work?

05:59.050 --> 06:00.950
Totally!

06:01.510 --> 06:02.800
What do you think you're doing?

06:03.750 --> 06:05.910
Why are you here?
What's going on?

06:05.910 --> 06:09.470
Because Sousuke told me
to help with his band.

06:09.470 --> 06:12.460
Well, then, can we do some
rehearsals, Motes-san?

06:12.460 --> 06:14.140
Why are you an eel?

06:14.140 --> 06:15.830
Squishy squirmy!

06:15.830 --> 06:16.540
Wolf!

06:16.840 --> 06:18.690
Quit being silly!

06:19.120 --> 06:22.440
Get over here and help with the gyoza stall.

06:25.430 --> 06:27.860
Listen up! This is a school!

06:28.190 --> 06:31.620
This is not a place for silly
grown-ups to come and hang out!

06:32.010 --> 06:34.570
Wait. The boy told me to—

06:33.560 --> 06:35.370
I never allowed it.

06:35.370 --> 06:37.180
Go home, right now.

06:37.180 --> 06:38.850
They can't.

06:38.850 --> 06:40.570
They're finally here.

06:40.570 --> 06:42.610
What do you think is
going to happen when they

06:42.610 --> 06:44.550
find out that some strange
men are in the building?

06:44.550 --> 06:45.910
It'll be a huge—

06:45.090 --> 06:45.910
Why?!

06:45.910 --> 06:47.380
Why won't you confess to him?

06:47.640 --> 06:51.550
I don't know if he likes me or not.

06:51.550 --> 06:53.640
Release your love. Your love!

06:54.170 --> 06:55.500
Not for him.

06:55.800 --> 06:57.140
For yourself!

06:58.600 --> 06:59.850
Li-chan!

07:00.170 --> 07:01.180
Yes!

07:01.650 --> 07:03.520
Yes!

07:03.920 --> 07:04.940
Listen!

07:05.240 --> 07:07.650
I'm going to say it again! This is a school.

07:07.650 --> 07:11.650
It's not a place for nuisances like you,

07:11.650 --> 07:13.530
who never think about
anything but yourselves!

07:13.820 --> 07:16.920
I'm sorry, but I can't go home
yet, my little kitten.

07:16.920 --> 07:17.790
You see...

07:18.190 --> 07:20.110
I haven't finished teaching

07:20.110 --> 07:22.920
the girls what true love is!

07:23.650 --> 07:25.320
Who <i>are</i> you?

07:25.320 --> 07:27.420
Where did you pick up that sense of duty?

07:27.420 --> 07:29.980
I have the cosplay café, too.

07:29.980 --> 07:31.840
I have my gyoza stall.

07:31.840 --> 07:34.010
Why are you three even here?

07:34.010 --> 07:36.180
I asked you to start a
band with me, didn't I?

07:36.520 --> 07:38.640
Just get out of here, now.

07:37.850 --> 07:40.680
Chopin-niisan, to be honest,

07:40.980 --> 07:43.310
I can't keep up with the
school festival atmosphere.

07:43.700 --> 07:44.740
I know.

07:44.740 --> 07:48.020
To hell with that giddy crap, right?

07:48.740 --> 07:50.150
Chopin-niisan!

07:49.220 --> 07:50.150
Yes!

07:50.630 --> 07:52.150
Yes!

07:52.580 --> 07:54.590
All right, fine.

07:54.590 --> 07:57.080
You can stay at school.

07:57.620 --> 08:01.000
Just don't do anything
that'll draw attention.

08:01.300 --> 08:03.150
I'm going to end up being
the one to deal with it.

08:02.440 --> 08:03.920
Why?

08:03.920 --> 08:05.220
It's a school festival.

08:05.220 --> 08:07.160
Who cares what it is if it's fun?

08:07.160 --> 08:07.960
No.

08:07.960 --> 08:10.220
School activities have to be moderate.

08:10.220 --> 08:11.670
There, there.

08:12.020 --> 08:13.720
Calm down, you two.

08:13.720 --> 08:15.980
You're not going to have
any fun if you're fighting,

08:15.980 --> 08:17.520
nor are you going to keep it moderate.

08:17.520 --> 08:18.570
Let's talk it over.

08:18.870 --> 08:20.830
For a great school festival.

08:22.230 --> 08:25.850
Yes, yes!

08:22.900 --> 08:25.240
He talks like a teacher.

08:25.240 --> 08:26.990
This year's school festival

08:26.990 --> 08:29.530
will go well with him
here, right, Principal?

08:30.990 --> 08:33.280
What's going on?

08:33.490 --> 08:34.860
Cosplay Cafe

08:33.670 --> 08:34.860
What's going on?

08:35.080 --> 08:37.830
What? How did this happen?

08:36.570 --> 08:37.830
Liszt's Love

08:38.140 --> 08:39.030
Why?!

08:39.030 --> 08:40.490
Cooperation
Order
Success!

08:39.030 --> 08:40.490
School festivals call for:
Friendship!
Courage!

08:39.380 --> 08:40.490
Why?

08:40.770 --> 08:43.410
How could this happen?!

08:43.840 --> 08:45.250
Motes!

08:45.250 --> 08:46.830
Beethes-san!

08:47.070 --> 08:48.500
Li-chan!

08:48.800 --> 08:50.920
Chopin-niisan.

08:50.380 --> 08:52.380
Schu-sensei

08:50.920 --> 08:52.380
Schu-sensei!

08:52.820 --> 08:55.350
It's a nightmare. Unbelievable.

08:55.680 --> 08:57.640
Guys, hear me out.

08:58.070 --> 09:01.640
I, Kagura Sousuke, have
an announcement to make.

09:02.310 --> 09:04.700
I will be forming a band for the

09:04.700 --> 09:06.870
upcoming school festival concert

09:06.870 --> 09:09.550
and showing off my original song.

09:11.000 --> 09:12.400
With them?

09:12.400 --> 09:14.300
You were serious about the band?

09:14.300 --> 09:16.570
Sorry I doubted you, Kagura-kun.

09:19.330 --> 09:24.620
Kagura! Kagura!

09:21.340 --> 09:22.470
It's a miracle!

09:23.020 --> 09:24.620
I can't believe it.

09:24.940 --> 09:26.660
This is it!

09:26.660 --> 09:28.220
This is what I was looking for.

09:28.220 --> 09:31.450
It's finally my time!

09:31.950 --> 09:33.840
Let's do this! I'll do it this time!

09:34.180 --> 09:37.940
It's Kagura Sousuke's time to shine!

09:55.360 --> 09:56.650
Today's the day!

10:02.580 --> 10:04.410
"I can't take it" - Claskey Klasky

10:12.180 --> 10:14.800
Bach-sama, those ClassicaLoids

10:14.800 --> 10:16.340
are up to something.

10:16.710 --> 10:18.970
They're talking about starting a band.

10:19.560 --> 10:22.230
What might happen in a band

10:22.230 --> 10:24.740
with five of the Eight Sounds?

10:26.600 --> 10:28.350
Basic Programming

10:40.030 --> 10:41.910
School Festival in 1 Day

10:46.550 --> 10:47.660
Guys, can I say something?

10:47.890 --> 10:48.780
Go ahead.

10:50.350 --> 10:51.390
Here I go.

10:51.390 --> 10:52.040
Go.

10:54.230 --> 10:55.170
I'm really going to go.

10:55.440 --> 10:56.470
Hurry!

10:57.140 --> 10:58.980
Okay, here we go.

11:11.900 --> 11:13.230
What? How?

11:14.360 --> 11:15.480
Principal's Office

11:15.480 --> 11:17.180
My stomach...

11:17.180 --> 11:18.650
What's wrong, Principal?

11:19.780 --> 11:20.650
Cosplay Cafe

11:25.290 --> 11:27.070
What do you think?

11:27.070 --> 11:28.160
It's pretty good, isn't it?

11:28.660 --> 11:30.930
I worked really hard on it.

11:33.230 --> 11:35.880
Pfft, what's the matter?

11:35.880 --> 11:39.270
At a loss for words because
it's so high-quality?

11:39.270 --> 11:40.800
Oh, man.

11:41.300 --> 11:45.240
Don't you think there's some room for
improvement on this piece, though?

11:45.240 --> 11:48.640
I want you guys to tell
me what you really think.

11:49.570 --> 11:51.380
Wh-What do we do with him?

11:51.380 --> 11:53.880
He wants an honest opinion.

11:53.880 --> 11:55.190
Someone tell him.

11:55.190 --> 11:57.480
Hot pot would be nice tonight.

11:57.480 --> 11:58.750
Indeed.

11:58.750 --> 11:59.900
Don't run from the problem!

12:00.260 --> 12:02.720
Oh, so, how was the intro?

12:03.020 --> 12:05.120
I actually put a lot of thought into it.

12:05.380 --> 12:08.630
See? He's saying something crazy.

12:08.630 --> 12:10.190
Someone teach him something.

12:10.190 --> 12:12.160
Hey, how about kimchi hot pot?

12:12.160 --> 12:13.420
Splendid as always, Senpai.

12:13.420 --> 12:14.120
Hey!

12:15.210 --> 12:16.650
What's up, guys?

12:16.650 --> 12:19.250
I'm going to greenlight this music unless
anyone has anything to say about it.

12:19.490 --> 12:21.490
Hear that? He says he's
going to greenlight it.

12:21.490 --> 12:22.560
The horror!

12:22.560 --> 12:25.010
Say something, or we're going to

12:25.010 --> 12:27.440
end up having to play that piece in public!

12:28.390 --> 12:30.520
Cho-chan! Pretending to sleep? You coward!

12:32.350 --> 12:33.290
Okay,

12:34.040 --> 12:35.190
I'll say it.

12:35.670 --> 12:37.480
Sousuke, what's up with this song?

12:37.480 --> 12:38.390
It's terrible.

12:38.750 --> 12:40.440
I can't stand listening to it.

12:43.130 --> 12:44.670
Did you actually study?

12:44.670 --> 12:46.940
It's terrible from the bottom up.

12:46.940 --> 12:50.080
You're just kind of throwing
it together as it comes.

12:50.680 --> 12:52.970
You're not going to touch
people's hearts that way.

12:53.740 --> 12:56.710
You imitated something, didn't you?

12:56.710 --> 12:59.120
It sounds familiar.

12:59.940 --> 13:02.300
I can tell, you know.

13:03.130 --> 13:03.890
He said it.

13:03.890 --> 13:04.700
All of it!

13:04.700 --> 13:05.520
Wolf...

13:05.520 --> 13:07.090
You barbarian!

13:07.090 --> 13:08.720
Please, have some sense!

13:08.960 --> 13:11.660
Come on, Motes, you don't
have to say it like that.

13:11.660 --> 13:14.800
But he asked for an honest opinion.

13:14.800 --> 13:16.640
But still...

13:19.180 --> 13:20.910
I-I know, right?

13:21.500 --> 13:22.910
It's terrible, right?

13:23.370 --> 13:25.070
Can't stand listening to it, huh?

13:26.820 --> 13:29.850
I-I'm no match for the geniuses.

13:30.560 --> 13:32.400
You guys write the music.

13:32.740 --> 13:35.210
I think the audience will appreciate
it more that way, too.

13:35.610 --> 13:38.160
Oh, and you have your Musik.

13:38.700 --> 13:41.340
I'm sure that'll get the crowd pumped up.

13:41.340 --> 13:42.260
Sousuke.

13:43.430 --> 13:45.470
Are you okay with that?

13:52.510 --> 13:53.580
What does it matter?

13:53.580 --> 13:55.060
Hey, it's Motes-kun.

13:55.380 --> 13:57.160
You were here, Beethes-san?

13:57.160 --> 13:59.190
Are you practicing for that band?

13:59.480 --> 14:01.320
Hey, play us a song.

14:01.320 --> 14:02.570
Nice, a jam session.

14:02.880 --> 14:04.540
Please. Play a song.

14:04.540 --> 14:05.900
Play some music!

14:05.900 --> 14:11.870
Music! Music! Music!

14:10.140 --> 14:11.410
S-Sorry...

15:03.450 --> 15:04.470
Motes-kun!

15:04.470 --> 15:05.370
Beethes-san!

15:05.370 --> 15:06.050
Li-chan!

15:06.050 --> 15:06.760
Chopin-niisan!

15:06.760 --> 15:08.170
Schu-sensei!

15:12.640 --> 15:13.550
Sousuke!

15:21.430 --> 15:23.690
That tool's not coming home.

15:24.120 --> 15:26.030
Looks like he's not at
his own place, either.

15:26.940 --> 15:29.340
I wonder what's wrong with him.

15:29.340 --> 15:30.870
Did something happen?

15:30.870 --> 15:33.390
Wh—You seriously can't tell?

15:33.390 --> 15:34.180
What?!

15:38.410 --> 15:39.400
'Sup?

15:43.180 --> 15:44.920
What is it, Beethes?

15:47.100 --> 15:48.120
Beethes?

15:48.570 --> 15:52.370
I <i>am</i> worried about how the
boy is doing right now.

15:52.940 --> 15:54.350
But it's almost time.

15:54.920 --> 15:55.600
Huh?

15:55.980 --> 15:57.420
It's almost...

15:59.380 --> 16:00.500
You're right.

16:03.010 --> 16:05.440
Sousuke, I'm a machine,

16:05.440 --> 16:07.820
so I'm not good at guessing your emotions.

16:08.360 --> 16:10.540
But may I say one thing?

16:10.900 --> 16:13.390
You're really pathetic right now.

16:13.390 --> 16:14.270
Shut up.

16:14.270 --> 16:15.930
Totally sad.

16:15.930 --> 16:16.990
Shut up.

16:16.990 --> 16:19.800
Was it really cruel, what Motes-san said?

16:19.800 --> 16:21.740
I don't think it was.

16:21.740 --> 16:23.710
What he said was accurate,

16:23.710 --> 16:25.970
pertinent, and very much on-point.

16:25.970 --> 16:29.030
I wouldn't expect less from
the acclaimed "child prodigy"

16:29.030 --> 16:32.160
whose music is loved two
hundred years later.

16:32.160 --> 16:33.880
He's out of your league.

16:33.880 --> 16:37.010
Way too much to justify a student
beginner like you getting so upset.

16:37.010 --> 16:38.430
Is that supposed to make me feel better?

16:38.430 --> 16:39.410
Nope.

16:41.260 --> 16:42.600
Damn it!

16:42.980 --> 16:44.370
Damn it!

16:44.730 --> 16:46.260
Come on.

16:46.260 --> 16:49.070
I tried really hard.

16:49.580 --> 16:52.490
What will you do? The concert is tomorrow.

16:53.440 --> 16:55.140
Let's give up for this year.

16:55.140 --> 16:57.370
You still have next year.

17:04.340 --> 17:05.250
No way.

17:05.520 --> 17:06.490
What?

17:06.490 --> 17:09.050
No. I'm not waiting until next year.

17:10.430 --> 17:11.690
Hurry up.

17:11.690 --> 17:13.190
We're going to go find him.

17:13.190 --> 17:15.220
I'm too lazy.

17:15.220 --> 17:17.900
Plus I'm getting hungry.

17:17.900 --> 17:20.720
Wolf, the boy is still a minor.

17:20.720 --> 17:21.940
Why are you eating?

17:21.940 --> 17:24.180
No fair! Give me some!

17:23.300 --> 17:24.700
Wolf! What are you —

17:29.310 --> 17:31.010
S-Sousuke...

17:32.320 --> 17:34.930
I'm breaking up the band.

17:36.880 --> 17:38.930
I'm performing alone tomorrow.

17:41.620 --> 17:45.620
I can get chicks if I try, too, you know!

17:45.850 --> 17:47.600
Stupid!

17:59.020 --> 18:01.390
Sorry about the inconvenience.

18:01.690 --> 18:05.870
But since those lot are showing
up together in public,

18:05.870 --> 18:08.090
we're going to have to keep an eye on them.

18:08.430 --> 18:11.230
Who knows what they might do.

18:11.230 --> 18:15.940
Festival

18:12.030 --> 18:14.630
Those idiot ClassicaLoids...

18:15.940 --> 18:18.950
Haunted House

18:18.950 --> 18:20.160
Cosplay Café

18:23.950 --> 18:26.940
Potatoes! Potatoes!

18:26.500 --> 18:30.630
Baked Potatoes

18:26.940 --> 18:29.810
Potatoes by former Claskey
Klasky member Tchaiko-chan!

18:29.810 --> 18:32.710
They're great!

18:34.210 --> 18:34.840
See?

18:37.450 --> 18:40.710
I need to put food on my plate!
Let go!

18:40.710 --> 18:44.430
Everyone, they're abducting
an innocent girl!

18:44.430 --> 18:46.930
Festival

18:47.530 --> 18:49.100
Did you see the tool?

18:49.100 --> 18:51.990
No. I don't think he's here.

18:52.360 --> 18:55.530
Good for him for fighting back,
but did he end up running away?

18:56.460 --> 18:58.200
No, he didn't run.

18:59.530 --> 19:01.210
He's here. See?

19:09.960 --> 19:11.960
What is that?

19:13.050 --> 19:15.310
My name is Kagura Sousuke.

19:15.930 --> 19:19.050
First, there's something I need to tell you.

19:19.570 --> 19:21.880
I broke up the band.

19:22.360 --> 19:24.790
The other guys aren't going
to be on stage today.

19:24.790 --> 19:25.930
Really?

19:25.930 --> 19:26.770
They aren't coming?

19:26.770 --> 19:27.860
What about Beethes-san?

19:26.770 --> 19:28.600
I wanted to see Motes-san.

19:28.600 --> 19:31.360
But I did write a song.

19:32.320 --> 19:35.520
I wrote a song without anyone's
help and without copying anyone.

19:36.260 --> 19:37.220
Here I go.

19:53.320 --> 19:56.650
My name is Sousuke

19:56.650 --> 19:59.970
I've got nothing going for me

19:59.970 --> 20:03.340
My name is Sousuke

20:03.340 --> 20:06.570
I'm empty inside

20:06.570 --> 20:13.620
I'm talentless, plainest of the
plainest of the plainest of the plain

20:14.940 --> 20:18.340
I can't even make myself try,

20:18.340 --> 20:21.990
just the plainest of the plainest
of the plainest of the plain

20:23.280 --> 20:30.010
I don't want to be this way,
but this is the way I am

20:30.010 --> 20:33.760
I want to change someday

20:33.760 --> 20:38.250
But I'm all talk, no walk

20:44.940 --> 20:48.180
My name is Sousuke

20:46.590 --> 20:48.180
Wh-What's going on?

20:48.180 --> 20:51.540
I've got nothing going for me

20:48.460 --> 20:49.410
No.

20:49.980 --> 20:52.370
No... This can't be the boy's...

20:51.540 --> 20:55.060
My name is Sousuke

20:53.060 --> 20:54.690
Musik!

20:55.060 --> 20:58.340
I'm empty inside

20:57.330 --> 20:59.940
I can't believe it would have come to this.

20:58.340 --> 21:05.220
I'm talentless, plainest of the
plainest of the plainest of the plain

21:00.770 --> 21:01.790
Darkness!

21:01.790 --> 21:03.000
Darkness!

21:04.400 --> 21:06.400
Sousuke!

21:06.700 --> 21:09.900
I can't even make myself try,

21:09.900 --> 21:13.600
just the plainest of the plainest
of the plainest of the plain

21:12.670 --> 21:14.900
B-Bach-sama...

21:15.180 --> 21:21.780
I don't want to be this way,
but this is the way I am

21:15.510 --> 21:18.290
Save me!

21:21.780 --> 21:25.440
I want to change someday

21:25.440 --> 21:30.320
But I'm all talk, no walk

21:41.860 --> 21:43.940
K-Kagura-san! Hang in there!

21:43.940 --> 21:45.230
Onii-chan...

21:45.230 --> 21:46.840
Stop...

21:46.840 --> 21:47.820
Kagura-san!

21:51.980 --> 21:53.410
Are you okay?

21:53.710 --> 21:55.410
I thought I was dead,

21:55.410 --> 21:56.670
even though I'm a machine.

21:57.210 --> 21:58.850
That was horrifying.

21:58.850 --> 22:01.210
I think it ended well, though.

22:01.210 --> 22:03.070
He wanted to be popular.

22:03.070 --> 22:04.580
That was awesome, Kagura-kun!

22:04.580 --> 22:05.720
That was hilarious!

22:04.820 --> 22:07.550
Sing it again, come on!

22:08.650 --> 22:13.260
Kagura! Kagura! Kagura!

22:13.260 --> 22:16.470
My name is Sousuke

22:16.470 --> 22:18.980
I've got nothing going for me

22:18.980 --> 22:20.440
Dude, it's not <i>that</i> funny!

22:20.780 --> 22:23.800
I don't even get it.

22:23.800 --> 22:25.320
Why did you even sing that shit?

22:27.030 --> 22:28.060
I don't know.

22:28.360 --> 22:29.990
I just tried my best.

22:31.760 --> 22:33.580
Tried to do <i>what</i>?

24:15.970 --> 24:25.060
Episode 16: Work,
Beethes! Motes!

24:16.730 --> 24:18.710
It's all in the name: Otowakan.

24:18.710 --> 24:22.350
A tattered old shack, but
there's no place like home.

24:22.350 --> 24:24.290
Its only flaw is that one must pay rent.

24:24.290 --> 24:26.300
The landlord's demands are hard and arduous.

24:26.300 --> 24:29.040
Oh, what I would do for money...
